 <iati-activity default-currency="EUR" hierarchy="2" humanitarian="1" iati-activities:version="2.02" xml:lang="EN" xmlns:iati-activities="http://d-portal.org/xmlns/iati-activities" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
  <iati-identifier>NL-KVK-40409352-PRJ13-123-0007</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="NL-KVK-40409352" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Netherlands Red Cross</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Chronic Crisis Sudan: Addressing Food Insecurity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project plan should be read in conjunction with the Regional Hunger Crisis which provides an overarching operational and accountability framework for all countries as part of the Regional Appeal. SRCS intervention strategy is primarily to respond effectively to the unfolding emergency and promote self-reliance through the priority sectors of food security, WASH and health and nutrition of those affected by hunger.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The total estimated number of beneficiaries amounts to 164.740 people in food insecure communities (IPC 3 or IPC 4) in Geneina, Habila, Sirba and Jebel Moon.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will focus on 4 localities where SRCS has already been working the past few years with support of NLRC, including Geneina (661,666), Habila (135,256), Sirba (200,848), and Jebel Moon (70,226).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through an integrated approach, the project will reach food insecure communities through unconditional cash transfer and WASH as part of the short-term interventions. The mid-term outcome focuses on increasing food and water system stability through inter-communal natural resource management and construction of a multi-purpose water system.</narrative>
  </description>
